{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563354-first-session-1st-edition-vtm-with-my-first-group-highlights","id":1563354,"title":"First session 1st Edition VtM with my first group Highlights","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-08-22T18:21:14-07:00","id":1563354,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon11.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> First session 1st Edition VtM with my first group Highlights","content":"Just a rundown of some fun and funny things that transpired:<br /> <br /> 1. Malkavian Herald seemingly teleporting around to gather the PC's <br /> <br /> 2. PC's attempting to blend in to human areas like a coffee shop, only to throw out full cups of coffee to the chagrin of the teenagers working the counter <br /> <br /> 3. Nosforatu PC Injuring himself in a frenzy after wasting nearly all his blood points on vanish and thousand faces after finding out he didn't have to do any of that and they were never going to sit and discuss confidential info in a mortal coffee shop<br /> <br /> 4. The same nosforatu damaging our ventrue's car window in said frenzy in an attempt to headbutt our tremere that caused the incident (he managed a full dodge roll) <br /> <br /> 5. Our tremere ordering a scrawny blood doll at a brujah bar for our nosforatu<br /> <br /> 6. Our Tremere and Ventrue getting their asses kicked in a game of pool with a Brujah coupe on the very verge of frenzy because the PC's couldn't keep their mouths shut<br /> <br /> 7. Our nosforatu watching all this while &quot;eating&quot; peanuts (chewing and spitting them out)<br /> <br /> overall a fun sesh and I really feel like my characters are believable working through being first time vampires really well!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29128-internetflexing","name":"Internetflexing","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-23T02:52:32-07:00","id":1563362,"title":"","content":"VtM works surprisingly well to run entire sessions of PCs getting sidetracked by problems they arranged for themselves with no bearing in the main plot. Depending on the group your players can easily cause 60 to 80% of everything they have to deal with, greatly freeing you from planning plots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-23T13:25:53-07:00","id":1563373,"title":"","content":"Trying to headbutt a Tremere seems like a measured response, compared to what most folks want to do with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}